{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI FINDING — one extra file was unavoidable, and it is DERIVED, not hand-edited. Patch set 1 of\nGerrit 1240 took a Verified -1 whose real cause was NOT pip-audit: the \"Env-var registry drift\ngate\" in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml (~:322) regenerates docs/env-vars.md with\nscripts/gen_env_registry.py and fails on any diff. That registry records the LINE NUMBER of every\nenv-var read under src/rebar, and my import block in adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py shifted its\nnon-literal os.environ.get read from :41 to :49 — a one-line delta:\n\n  - src/.../adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:41 — os.environ.get(<non-literal>)\n  + src/.../adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:49 — os.environ.get(<non-literal>)\n\nReproduced locally, regenerated with the gate's own command, and folded into patch set 2 of the\nFIRST change (1240) — the one that shifts the line — rather than added as a third commit, so each\nchange stays independently green. Recording it because this is a non-obvious coupling that will\nbite every future contributor who inserts or deletes lines above an env-var read: any such change\nmust re-run scripts/gen_env_registry.py even when it touches no env-var behaviour whatsoever.\n\nBoth changes are now at patch set 2. The only remaining failure is the pre-existing repo-wide\npip-audit block on click 8.2.1 / PYSEC-2026-2132 (ticket e47e-a33d-b9cf-4421), which is not mine\nand not recheckable; uv.lock and the workflows were not touched."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785713989195367001,"uuid":"c6d709e4-347a-446f-9476-0599c3bf5993"}